#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) is implemented in the context of solving the ground state of a nitrogen molecule."
msgstr "Diagonalisasi kuantum berasaskan sampel (SQD) dilaksanakan dalam konteks penyelesaian keadaan tanah molekul nitrogen."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQD Implementation"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan SQD"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore fontdict fontsize milli hcore ccsd Motta */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore fontdict fontsize milli hcore ccsd Motta */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQD for energy estimation of a chemistry Hamiltonian {#sqd-for-energy-estimation-of-a-chemistry-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "SQD untuk anggaran tenaga Hamiltonian kimia {#sqd-for-energy-estimation-of-a-chemistry-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this lesson, we will apply SQD to estimate the ground state energy of a molecule.\n"
msgstr "Dalam pelajaran ini, kita akan menerapkan SQD untuk menganggar tenaga keadaan tanah sebuah molekul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, we will discuss the following topics using the $4$-step Qiskit pattern approach:\n"
msgstr "Secara khusus, kita akan membincangkan topik berikut menggunakan pendekatan corak Qiskit $4$-langkah:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map problem to quantum circuits and operators\n"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan masalah kepada litar kuantum dan operator\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup the molecular Hamiltonian for $N_2$.\n"
msgstr "Sediakan Hamiltonian molekul untuk $N_2$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explain the chemistry-inspired and hardware-friendly local unitary cluster Jastrow (LUCJ) [\\[1\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr "Terangkan ansatz cluster Jastrow unitari setempat (LUCJ) yang terinspirasi kimia dan mesra perkakasan [\\[1\\]](#references)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize for target hardware\n"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan untuk perkakasan sasaran\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize gate counts and layout of the ansatz for hardware execution\n"
msgstr "Optimumkan bilangan gate dan susun atur ansatz untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute on target hardware\n"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan pada perkakasan sasaran\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the optimized circuit on a real QPU to generate samples of the subspace.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan litar yang dioptimumkan pada QPU sebenar untuk menjana sampel subruang.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process results\n"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses keputusan\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduce the self-consistent configuration recovery loop [\\[2\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr "Perkenalkan gelung pemulihan konfigurasi konsisten diri [\\[2\\]](#references)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process the full set of bitstring samples, using prior knowledge of particle number and the average orbital occupancy calculated on the most recent iteration.\n"
msgstr "Pasca-proses set penuh sampel bitstring, menggunakan pengetahuan terdahulu tentang bilangan zarah dan purata penghunian orbital yang dikira pada iterasi terbaru.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistically create batches of subsamples from recovered bitstrings.\n"
msgstr "Buat batch subsampel secara kebarangkalian daripada bitstring yang dipulihkan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Project and diagonalize the molecular Hamiltonian over each sampled subspace.\n"
msgstr "Unjurkan dan diagonalisasikan Hamiltonian molekul ke atas setiap subruang yang disampling.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save the minimum ground state energy found across all batches and update the avg orbital occupancy.\n"
msgstr "Simpan tenaga keadaan tanah minimum yang dijumpai merentasi semua batch dan kemas kini purata penghunian orbital.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will use several software packages throughout the lesson.\n"
"- `PySCF` to define the molecule and setup the Hamiltonian.\n"
"- `ffsim` package to construct the LUCJ ansatz.\n"
"- `Qiskit` for transpiling the ansatz for hardware execution.\n"
"- `Qiskit IBM Runtime` to execute the circuit on a QPU and collect samples.\n"
"- `Qiskit addon SQD` configuration recovery and ground state energy estimation using subspace projection and matrix diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan menggunakan beberapa pakej perisian sepanjang pelajaran.\n"
"- `PySCF` untuk mendefinisikan molekul dan menyediakan Hamiltonian.\n"
"- pakej `ffsim` untuk membina ansatz LUCJ.\n"
"- `Qiskit` untuk mentranspil ansatz untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan.\n"
"- `Qiskit IBM Runtime` untuk melaksanakan litar pada QPU dan mengumpul sampel.\n"
"- `Qiskit addon SQD` pemulihan konfigurasi dan anggaran tenaga keadaan tanah menggunakan unjuran subruang dan diagonalisasi matriks.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Map problem to quantum circuits and operators {#1-map-problem-to-quantum-circuits-and-operators}"
msgstr "1. Petakan masalah kepada litar kuantum dan operator {#1-map-problem-to-quantum-circuits-and-operators}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Molecular Hamiltonian {#molecular-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Hamiltonian Molekul {#molecular-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A molecular Hamiltonian takes the generic form:\n"
msgstr "Hamiltonian molekul mengambil bentuk generik:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{ \\substack{pr\\\\\\sigma} } h_{pr} \\, \\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma} \\hat{a}_{r\\sigma}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{ \\substack{prqs\\\\\\sigma\\tau} }\n"
"\\frac{(pr|qs)}{2} \\,\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma}\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{q\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{s\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{r\\sigma}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{ \\substack{pr\\\\\\sigma} } h_{pr} \\, \\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma} \\hat{a}_{r\\sigma}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{ \\substack{prqs\\\\\\sigma\\tau} }\n"
"\\frac{(pr|qs)}{2} \\,\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma}\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{q\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{s\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{r\\sigma}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma}$/$\\hat{a}_{p\\sigma}$ are the fermionic creation/annihilation operators associated to the $p$-th basis set element and the spin $\\sigma$. $h_{pr}$ and $(pr|qs)$ are the one- and two-body electronic integrals. Using pySCF, we will define the molecule and compute the one- and two-body integrals of the Hamiltonian for basis set `6-31g`.\n"
msgstr "$\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma}$/$\\hat{a}_{p\\sigma}$ ialah operator penciptaan/pemusnahan fermionis yang berkaitan dengan elemen set asas ke-$p$ dan spin $\\sigma$. $h_{pr}$ dan $(pr|qs)$ ialah kamiran elektronik satu dan dua jasad. Menggunakan pySCF, kita akan mendefinisikan molekul dan mengira kamiran satu dan dua jasad Hamiltonian untuk set asas `6-31g`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this lesson, we will use Jordan-Wigner (JW) transformation to map a fermionic wavefunction to a qubit wavefunction so that it can be prepared using a quantum circuit. The JW transformation maps the Fock space of fermions in M spatial orbitals onto the Hilbert space of 2M qubits, that is, a spatial orbital is split into two _spin orbitals_, one associated with a spin up ($\\alpha$) electron and another with spin down ($\\beta$). A spin orbital can be occupied or unoccupied. Usually, when we refer to number of orbitals, we will be using number of _spatial_ orbitals. The number of spin orbitals will be double. In quantum circuits, we will represent each spin orbital with one qubit. Thus, a set of qubits will represent spin-up or $\\alpha$-orbitals, and another set will represent spin-down or $\\beta$-orbitals. For example, $N_2$ molecule for `6-31g` basis set has $16$ spatial orbitals (that is, $16$ $\\alpha$ + $16$ $\\beta$ = $32$ spin orbitals). Thus, we will need a $32$-qubit quantum circuit (we may need extra ancilla qubits as discussed later). The qubits are measured in computational basis to generate bitstrings, which represent electronic configurations or (Slater) determinants. Throughout this lesson, we will use the terms bitstrings, configurations, and determinants interchangeably. The bitstrings tell us electron occupancy in spin orbitals: a $1$ in a bit position means the corresponding spin orbital is occupied, while a $0$ means the spin orbital is empty. As electronic structure problems are particle preserving, only a fixed number of spin orbitals must be occupied. The $N_2$ molecule has $5$ spin-up ($\\alpha$) and $5$ spin-down ($\\beta$) electrons. Thus, any bitstring representing the $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ orbitals must have five $1\\text{s}$ each for $N_2$ molecule.\n"
msgstr "Dalam pelajaran ini, kita akan menggunakan transformasi Jordan-Wigner (JW) untuk memetakan fungsi gelombang fermionis kepada fungsi gelombang qubit supaya ia boleh disediakan menggunakan litar kuantum. Transformasi JW memetakan ruang Fock fermion dalam M orbital ruang ke ruang Hilbert 2M qubit, iaitu, orbital ruang dibahagikan kepada dua _orbital spin_, satu yang berkaitan dengan elektron spin atas ($\\alpha$) dan satu lagi spin bawah ($\\beta$). Orbital spin boleh dihuni atau tidak dihuni. Biasanya, apabila kita merujuk kepada bilangan orbital, kita menggunakan bilangan orbital _ruang_. Bilangan orbital spin akan menjadi dua kali ganda. Dalam litar kuantum, kita akan mewakili setiap orbital spin dengan satu qubit. Oleh itu, satu set qubit akan mewakili orbital spin atas atau $\\alpha$, dan set lain akan mewakili orbital spin bawah atau $\\beta$. Sebagai contoh, molekul $N_2$ untuk set asas `6-31g` mempunyai $16$ orbital ruang (iaitu, $16$ $\\alpha$ + $16$ $\\beta$ = $32$ orbital spin). Oleh itu, kita memerlukan litar kuantum $32$-Qubit (kita mungkin memerlukan qubit ancilla tambahan seperti yang dibincangkan kemudian). Qubit diukur dalam asas pengkomputeran untuk menjana bitstring, yang mewakili konfigurasi elektronik atau determinan (Slater). Sepanjang pelajaran ini, kita akan menggunakan istilah bitstring, konfigurasi, dan determinan secara bergantian. Bitstring memberitahu kita penghunian elektron dalam orbital spin: $1$ dalam kedudukan bit bermakna orbital spin yang sepadan dihuni, manakala $0$ bermakna orbital spin kosong. Kerana masalah struktur elektronik memelihara zarah, hanya bilangan tetap orbital spin yang mesti dihuni. Molekul $N_2$ mempunyai $5$ elektron spin atas ($\\alpha$) dan $5$ elektron spin bawah ($\\beta$). Oleh itu, sebarang bitstring yang mewakili orbital $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ mesti mempunyai lima $1$ masing-masing untuk molekul $N_2$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.1 Quantum circuit for sample generation: The LUCJ ansatz {#11-quantum-circuit-for-sample-generation-the-lucj-ansatz}"
msgstr "1.1 Litar kuantum untuk penjanaan sampel: Ansatz LUCJ {#11-quantum-circuit-for-sample-generation-the-lucj-ansatz}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this lesson, we will use the local unitary coupled cluster Jastrow (LUCJ) [\\\\[1\\\\]](#references) ansatz for quantum state preparation and subsequent sampling. First, we will explain different building blocks of the full UCJ ansatz and the approximations made in the local version of it. Next, by using ffsim package, we will construct the LUCJ ansatz and optimize it using Qiskit transpiler for hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "Dalam pelajaran ini, kita akan menggunakan ansatz cluster Jastrow unitari setempat (LUCJ) [\\\\[1\\\\]](#references) untuk penyediaan keadaan kuantum dan pensampelan berikutnya. Pertama, kita akan menjelaskan blok-blok bangunan yang berbeza bagi ansatz UCJ penuh dan penghampiran yang dibuat dalam versi setempatnya. Seterusnya, dengan menggunakan pakej ffsim, kita akan membina ansatz LUCJ dan mengoptimumkannya menggunakan Transpiler Qiskit untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The UCJ ansatz has the following form (for a product of $L$ layers or repetitions of the UCJ operator.)\n"
msgstr "Ansatz UCJ mempunyai bentuk berikut (untuk produk $L$ lapisan atau ulangan operator UCJ.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\prod_{\\mu=1}^{L}{(e^{K^{\\mu}} \\times {e^{iJ^{\\mu}}} \\times {e^{-K^{\\mu}}})} |\\Phi_{0}\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\prod_{\\mu=1}^{L}{(e^{K^{\\mu}} \\times {e^{iJ^{\\mu}}} \\times {e^{-K^{\\mu}}})} |\\Phi_{0}\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where, $\\vert \\Phi_{0} \\rangle$ is a reference state, typically taken as the Hartree-Fock (HF) state. As the Hartree-Fock state is defined as having the lowest numbered orbitals occupied, the HF state preparation will involve applying X gates to set qubits corresponding to occupied orbitals to one. For example, the HF state preparation block for 4 spatial orbitals and 2 up- and 2 down-spin may look like the following:\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 8 qubits, 4 called alpha orbitals and 4 called beta orbitals. The top two alpha and the top two beta have a \"not\" gate.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig1.avif)\n"
"A single repetition of the UCJ operator ${(e^{K^{(\\mu)}} \\times {e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}} \\times {e^{-K^{(\\mu)}}})}$ consists of a diagonal Coulomb evolution ($e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$) sandwiched by orbital rotations ($e^{K^{(\\mu)}}$ and $e^{-K^{(\\mu)}}$).\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing that the UCJ circuit can be broken down into rotation layers and a diagonal Coulomb evolution layer.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig2.avif)\n"
"Orbital rotation blocks work on a single spin species ($\\alpha$ (up-spin)/$\\beta$ (down-spin)). For each electron species, orbital rotation consists of a layer of single-qubit $R_{z}$ gates followed by a sequence of 2-qubit Given's rotation gates ($XX + YY$ gates).\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana, $\\vert \\Phi_{0} \\rangle$ ialah keadaan rujukan, biasanya diambil sebagai keadaan Hartree-Fock (HF). Kerana keadaan Hartree-Fock ditakrifkan sebagai mempunyai orbital bernombor terendah yang dihuni, penyediaan keadaan HF akan melibatkan penerapan gate X untuk menetapkan qubit yang sepadan dengan orbital yang dihuni kepada satu. Sebagai contoh, blok penyediaan keadaan HF untuk 4 orbital ruang dan 2 spin atas dan 2 spin bawah mungkin kelihatan seperti berikut:\n"
"![Gambar rajah litar yang menunjukkan 8 qubit, 4 dipanggil orbital alfa dan 4 dipanggil orbital beta. Dua alfa atas dan dua beta atas masing-masing mempunyai gate \"not\".](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig1.avif)\n"
"Satu ulangan operator UCJ ${(e^{K^{(\\mu)}} \\times {e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}} \\times {e^{-K^{(\\mu)}}})}$ terdiri daripada evolusi Coulomb pepenjuru ($e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$) yang dikelilingi oleh putaran orbital ($e^{K^{(\\mu)}}$ dan $e^{-K^{(\\mu)}}$).\n"
"![Gambar rajah litar yang menunjukkan bahawa litar UCJ boleh dipecahkan kepada lapisan putaran dan lapisan evolusi Coulomb pepenjuru.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig2.avif)\n"
"Blok putaran orbital berfungsi pada satu spesies spin ($\\alpha$ (spin atas)/$\\beta$ (spin bawah)). Untuk setiap spesies elektron, putaran orbital terdiri daripada lapisan gate $R_{z}$ satu-qubit diikuti oleh urutan gate putaran Given's 2-qubit ($XX + YY$ gate).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 2-qubit gates act on adjacent spin-orbitals (nearest neighbor qubits), and therefore, are implementable on IBM&reg; QPUs without the need for SWAP gates.\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 4 alpha orbital qubits and 4 beta orbital qubits. The circuits start with R-Z gates, and then have a series of Given's rotation gates.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig3.avif)\n"
"The $e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$, also known as the diagonal Coulomb operator, consists of three blocks. Two of them work on same spin sectors ($e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\alpha}^{(\\mu)}}$ and $e^{iJ_{\\beta \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$), and one works between two spin sectors ($e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$).\n"
msgstr ""
"Gate 2-qubit bertindak pada orbital spin bersebelahan (qubit jiran terdekat), dan oleh itu, boleh dilaksanakan pada QPU IBM&reg; tanpa memerlukan gate SWAP.\n"
"![Gambar rajah litar yang menunjukkan 4 qubit orbital alfa dan 4 qubit orbital beta. Litar bermula dengan gate R-Z, dan kemudian mempunyai siri gate putaran Given's.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig3.avif)\n"
"$e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$, juga dikenali sebagai operator Coulomb pepenjuru, terdiri daripada tiga blok. Dua daripadanya berfungsi pada sektor spin yang sama ($e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\alpha}^{(\\mu)}}$ dan $e^{iJ_{\\beta \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$), dan satu berfungsi antara dua sektor spin ($e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All the blocks in $e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$ consists of number-number gates $U_{nn}(\\phi)$ [\\[1\\]](#references). A $U_{nn}(\\phi)$ gate can be further broken down into a $R_{ZZ}(\\frac{\\phi}{2})$ gate followed by two single-qubit $Rz(-\\frac{\\phi}{2})$ gates acting on two separate qubits.\n"
msgstr "Semua blok dalam $e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$ terdiri daripada gate nombor-nombor $U_{nn}(\\phi)$ [\\[1\\]](#references). Gate $U_{nn}(\\phi)$ boleh diurai lebih lanjut kepada gate $R_{ZZ}(\\frac{\\phi}{2})$ diikuti oleh dua gate $Rz(-\\frac{\\phi}{2})$ satu-qubit yang bertindak pada dua qubit berasingan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Same-spin components ($J_{\\alpha \\alpha}$ and $J_{\\beta \\beta}$) have $U_{nn}$ gates between all possible pairs of qubits. However, as superconducting QPUs have restrictive connectivity, qubits must be swapped to realize gates between non-adjacent qubits.\n"
msgstr "Komponen spin yang sama ($J_{\\alpha \\alpha}$ dan $J_{\\beta \\beta}$) mempunyai gate $U_{nn}$ antara semua pasangan qubit yang mungkin. Namun, kerana QPU superkonduktor mempunyai sambungan yang terhad, qubit mesti ditukar untuk merealisasikan gate antara qubit yang tidak bersebelahan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, consider the following $e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\alpha}^{(\\mu)}}$ (or $e^{iJ_{\\beta \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$) block for $N = 4$ spatial orbitals. For a linear qubit connectivity, the last three gates are not directly implementable as they work between non-adjacent qubits (for example, Q0 and Q2 are not directly connected). Therefore, we need SWAP gates to make them adjacent (following figure shows an example with $3$ SWAP gates).\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing linearly-coupled qubits and corresponding alpha/beta circuits.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig4.avif)\n"
"Next, the $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ implements gates between same indexed orbitals from different spin sectors (for example, between $0\\alpha$ and $0\\beta$). Similarly, if the qubits are not physically adjacent on a QPU, these gates will also require SWAPs.\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 4 alpha qubits connected to the 4 beta qubits.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig5.avif)\n"
"From the above discussion, the UCJ ansatz faces some hurdles for HW execution as it needs SWAP gates due to non-adjacent qubit interactions. The local variant of the UCJ ansatz, LUCJ, addresses this challenge by removing some $U_{nn}$ from the diagonal Coulomb operator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, pertimbangkan blok $e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\alpha}^{(\\mu)}}$ (atau $e^{iJ_{\\beta \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$) berikut untuk $N = 4$ orbital ruang. Untuk sambungan qubit linear, tiga gate terakhir tidak boleh dilaksanakan secara langsung kerana mereka berfungsi antara qubit yang tidak bersebelahan (sebagai contoh, Q0 dan Q2 tidak bersambung secara langsung). Oleh itu, kita memerlukan gate SWAP untuk menjadikannya bersebelahan (rajah berikut menunjukkan contoh dengan $3$ gate SWAP).\n"
"![Gambar rajah litar yang menunjukkan qubit yang disambungkan secara linear dan litar alfa/beta yang sepadan.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig4.avif)\n"
"Seterusnya, $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ melaksanakan gate antara orbital berindeks sama dari sektor spin yang berbeza (sebagai contoh, antara $0\\alpha$ dan $0\\beta$). Begitu juga, jika qubit tidak bersampingan secara fizikal pada QPU, gate ini juga akan memerlukan SWAP.\n"
"![Gambar rajah litar yang menunjukkan 4 qubit alfa bersambung kepada 4 qubit beta.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig5.avif)\n"
"Daripada perbincangan di atas, ansatz UCJ menghadapi beberapa cabaran untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kerana ia memerlukan gate SWAP disebabkan interaksi qubit yang tidak bersebelahan. Varian setempat ansatz UCJ, LUCJ, menangani cabaran ini dengan mengeluarkan beberapa $U_{nn}$ daripada operator Coulomb pepenjuru.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the same electron species blocks, $J_{\\alpha \\alpha}$ and $J_{\\beta \\beta}$), we only keep the $U_{nn}$ gates compatible with nearest-neighbor connectivity and remove gates between non-adjacent qubits in the LUCJ version. Following figure shows the LUCJ block after removal of non-adjacent gates.\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 4 alpha qubits and 4 beta qubits each with R-Z gates, followed by two-qubit gates.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig6.avif)\n"
"Next, the LUCJ version of the $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ block that works between different electron species can take different shape based on the device topology.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam blok spesies elektron yang sama, $J_{\\alpha \\alpha}$ dan $J_{\\beta \\beta}$), kita hanya menyimpan gate $U_{nn}$ yang serasi dengan sambungan jiran terdekat dan mengeluarkan gate antara qubit yang tidak bersebelahan dalam versi LUCJ. Rajah berikut menunjukkan blok LUCJ selepas penyingkiran gate yang tidak bersebelahan.\n"
"![Gambar rajah litar yang menunjukkan 4 qubit alfa dan 4 qubit beta masing-masing dengan gate R-Z, diikuti oleh gate dua-qubit.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig6.avif)\n"
"Seterusnya, versi LUCJ blok $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ yang berfungsi antara spesies elektron yang berbeza boleh mengambil bentuk berbeza berdasarkan topologi peranti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, also, the LUCJ version gets rid of non-compatible gates. The figure below shows variants of the $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ block for different qubit topology including grid, hexagonal, heavy-hex, and linear.\n"
msgstr "Di sini juga, versi LUCJ menyingkirkan gate yang tidak serasi. Rajah di bawah menunjukkan varian blok $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ untuk topologi qubit yang berbeza termasuk grid, heksagonal, heavy-hex, dan linear.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Square**: we can have $U_{nn}$ gates between all $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ orbitals without any SWAPs, and therefore, do not need to remove any $U_{nn}$ gates.\n"
msgstr "**Petak**: kita boleh mempunyai gate $U_{nn}$ antara semua orbital $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ tanpa sebarang SWAP, dan oleh itu, tidak perlu mengeluarkan sebarang gate $U_{nn}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Heavy-hex**: The $\\alpha$-$\\beta$ interactions are kept between every $4$-th indexed (such as the 0th, 4th, and 8th) spin orbitals and are _ancilla_ mediated, that is, we need ancilla qubits between the linear chains representing $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ orbitals. This arrangement needs a limited number of SWAPs.\n"
msgstr "**Heavy-hex**: Interaksi $\\alpha$-$\\beta$ dikekalkan antara setiap orbital berindeks ke-$4$ (seperti ke-0, ke-4, dan ke-8) dan dimediasi _ancilla_, iaitu, kita memerlukan qubit ancilla antara rantaian linear yang mewakili orbital $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$. Susunan ini memerlukan bilangan SWAP yang terhad.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Hexagonal**: Every other orbital, such as 0th, 2nd, and 4th indexed orbitals, becomes nearest neighbors when $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are laid out in two adjacent linear chains.\n"
msgstr "**Heksagonal**: Setiap orbital yang lain, seperti orbital berindeks ke-0, ke-2, dan ke-4, menjadi jiran terdekat apabila $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ disusun dalam dua rantaian linear bersebelahan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- **Linear**: Only one $\\alpha$ and one $\\beta$ orbital are connected, which means the $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ block will have only one gate.\n"
"![Connectivity diagrams for different qubit layouts. They show qubits arranged on a square grid, a hexagonal lattice, a heavy-hex lattice (hexagonal lattice with one extra qubit along each side of the hexagon), and a linear chain.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig7.avif)\n"
"While removing gates from the UCJ ansatz to construct the LUCJ version makes it more HW compatible, the ansatz loses some expressivity. Therefore, more repetitions ($L$) of the modified UCJ operator may be needed when using the LUCJ ansatz.\n"
msgstr ""
"- **Linear**: Hanya satu orbital $\\alpha$ dan satu $\\beta$ bersambung, bermakna blok $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ hanya akan mempunyai satu gate.\n"
"![Gambar sambungan untuk susun atur qubit yang berbeza. Mereka menunjukkan qubit yang disusun pada grid petak, kekisi heksagonal, kekisi heavy-hex (kekisi heksagonal dengan satu qubit tambahan di sepanjang setiap sisi heksagon), dan rantaian linear.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig7.avif)\n"
"Walaupun mengeluarkan gate daripada ansatz UCJ untuk membina versi LUCJ menjadikannya lebih serasi dengan perkakasan, ansatz kehilangan beberapa kebolehunyahan. Oleh itu, lebih banyak ulangan ($L$) operator UCJ yang dimodifikasi mungkin diperlukan apabila menggunakan ansatz LUCJ.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.2 LUCJ ansatz initialization {#12-lucj-ansatz-initialization}"
msgstr "1.2 Permulaan ansatz LUCJ {#12-lucj-ansatz-initialization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The LUCJ is a parameterized ansatz, and we need to initialize the parameters before hardware execution. One way to initialize ansatz is by using `t1` and `t2` amplitudes from classical coupled cluster singles and doubles (CCSD) method, where `t1` amplitudes are the coefficient of single excitation operators and `t2` amplitudes are for double excitation operators.\n"
msgstr "LUCJ ialah ansatz berparameter, dan kita perlu memulakan parameter sebelum pelaksanaan perkakasan. Satu cara untuk memulakan ansatz ialah dengan menggunakan amplitud `t1` dan `t2` daripada kaedah cluster tunggal dan ganda berpasangan (CCSD) klasik, di mana amplitud `t1` ialah pekali operator rangsangan tunggal dan amplitud `t2` adalah untuk operator rangsangan ganda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that while initializing the LUCJ ansatz with `t1` and `t2` amplitudes generate decent results, the ansatz parameters may need further optimization.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa walaupun memulakan ansatz LUCJ dengan amplitud `t1` dan `t2` menghasilkan keputusan yang baik, parameter ansatz mungkin memerlukan pengoptimuman lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.3 Constructing the LUCJ ansatz using `ffsim` {#13-constructing-the-lucj-ansatz-using-ffsim}"
msgstr "1.3 Membina ansatz LUCJ menggunakan `ffsim` {#13-constructing-the-lucj-ansatz-using-ffsim}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will use the [ffsim](https://github.com/qiskit-community/ffsim/tree/main) package to create and initialize the ansatz with `t1` and `t2` amplitudes computed above. Since our molecule has a closed-shell Hartree-Fock state, we will use the spin-balanced variant of the UCJ ansatz, [UCJOpSpinBalanced](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/ffsim.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced).\n"
msgstr "Kita akan menggunakan pakej [ffsim](https://github.com/qiskit-community/ffsim/tree/main) untuk mencipta dan memulakan ansatz dengan amplitud `t1` dan `t2` yang dikira di atas. Kerana molekul kita mempunyai keadaan Hartree-Fock bercangkerang tertutup, kita akan menggunakan varian ansatz UCJ yang seimbang spin, [UCJOpSpinBalanced](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/ffsim.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As IBM hardware has a heavy-hex topology, we will adopt the _zig-zag_ pattern used in [\\[1\\]](#references) and explained above for qubit interactions. In this pattern, orbitals (qubits) with the same spin are connected with a line topology (red and blue circles). Due to the heavy-hex topology, orbitals for different spins have connections between every 4th orbital, that is, the 0th, 4th, 8th, and so on (purple circles).\n"
msgstr "Kerana perkakasan IBM mempunyai topologi heavy-hex, kita akan menggunakan corak _zig-zag_ yang digunakan dalam [\\[1\\]](#references) dan dijelaskan di atas untuk interaksi qubit. Dalam corak ini, orbital (qubit) dengan spin yang sama disambungkan dengan topologi garis (bulatan merah dan biru). Disebabkan topologi heavy-hex, orbital untuk spin yang berbeza mempunyai sambungan antara setiap orbital ke-4, iaitu, ke-0, ke-4, ke-8, dan seterusnya (bulatan ungu).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A zig-zag pattern traced out along a heavy-hex lattice.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A zig-zag pattern traced out along a heavy-hex lattice.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig8.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The LUCJ ansatz with repeated layers can be optimized by merging some adjacent blocks. Consider a case for `n_reps=2`. The two orbital rotation blocks in the middle can be merged into a single orbital rotation block. The `ffsim` package has a pass manager named `ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT` to optimize the circuit by merging such adjacent blocks.\n"
"![A diagram showing layers of the LUCJ ansatz.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig9.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"Ansatz LUCJ dengan lapisan berulang boleh dioptimumkan dengan menggabungkan beberapa blok bersebelahan. Pertimbangkan kes untuk `n_reps=2`. Dua blok putaran orbital di tengah boleh digabungkan menjadi satu blok putaran orbital tunggal. Pakej `ffsim` mempunyai pengurus laluan bernama `ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT` untuk mengoptimumkan litar dengan menggabungkan blok bersebelahan sedemikian.\n"
"![Gambar rajah yang menunjukkan lapisan-lapisan ansatz LUCJ.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig9.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Optimize for target hardware {#2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"
msgstr "2. Optimumkan untuk perkakasan sasaran {#2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we fetch a backend of our choice. We will optimize our circuit for the backend, and then execute the optimized circuit on the same backend to generate samples for the subspace.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, kita ambil backend pilihan kita. Kita akan mengoptimumkan litar kita untuk backend tersebut, dan kemudian melaksanakan litar yang dioptimumkan pada backend yang sama untuk menjana sampel bagi subruang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we recommend the following steps to optimize the ansatz and make it hardware-compatible.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, kita cadangkan langkah-langkah berikut untuk mengoptimumkan ansatz dan menjadikannya serasi dengan perkakasan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select physical qubits (`initial_layout`) from the target hardware that adheres to the zig-zag pattern (two linear chains with ancilla qubit in-between them) described above. Laying out qubits in this pattern leads to an efficient hardware-compatible circuit with less gates.\n"
msgstr "Pilih qubit fizikal (`initial_layout`) dari perkakasan sasaran yang mengikut corak zig-zag (dua rantaian linear dengan qubit ancilla di antara mereka) yang diterangkan di atas. Menyusun qubit dalam corak ini menghasilkan litar yang cekap dan serasi perkakasan dengan lebih sedikit gate.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate a staged pass manager using the [`generate_preset_pass_manager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager) function from Qiskit with your choice of `backend` and `initial_layout`.\n"
msgstr "Jana pengurus laluan berperingkat menggunakan fungsi [`generate_preset_pass_manager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager) dari Qiskit dengan `backend` dan `initial_layout` pilihan anda.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the `pre_init` stage of your staged pass manager to `ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT`. `ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT` includes Qiskit transpiler passes that decompose gates into orbital rotations and then merges the orbital rotations, resulting in fewer gates in the final circuit.\n"
msgstr "Tetapkan peringkat `pre_init` pengurus laluan berperingkat anda kepada `ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT`. `ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT` merangkumi laluan Transpiler Qiskit yang mengurai gate kepada putaran orbital dan kemudian menggabungkan putaran orbital, menghasilkan lebih sedikit gate dalam litar akhir.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the pass manager on your circuit.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan pengurus laluan pada litar anda.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Execute on target hardware {#3-execute-on-target-hardware}"
msgstr "3. Laksanakan pada perkakasan sasaran {#3-execute-on-target-hardware}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After optimizing the circuit for hardware execution, we are ready to run it on the target hardware and collect samples for ground state energy estimation. As we only have one circuit, we will use the `qiskit-ibm-runtime` [Job execution mode](/guides/execution-modes) and execute our circuit.\n"
msgstr "Setelah mengoptimumkan litar untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan, kita bersedia untuk menjalankannya pada perkakasan sasaran dan mengumpul sampel untuk anggaran tenaga keadaan tanah. Kerana kita hanya mempunyai satu litar, kita akan menggunakan mod pelaksanaan Kerja [Job execution mode](/guides/execution-modes) dan melaksanakan litar kita menggunakan `qiskit-ibm-runtime`.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Post-process results {#4-post-process-results}"
msgstr "4. Pasca-proses keputusan {#4-post-process-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The post-processing part of the SQD workflow can be summarized using the following diagram.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian pasca-pemprosesan aliran kerja SQD boleh diringkaskan menggunakan gambar rajah berikut.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A flow chart showing how sampled states are used to determine ground state eigenvalues and eigenvectors.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig10.avif)\n"
"Sampling the LUCJ ansatz in the computational basis generates a pool of noisy configurations $\\tilde{\\mathcal{\\chi}}$, which are used in the post-processing routine. It involves a method called (details discussed later) _configuration recovery_ to probabilistically correct configurations with incorrect electron numbers. Configurations only with correct electron numbers $\\tilde{\\mathcal{\\chi}}_{R}$ are then subsampled and distributed into multiple batches based on the frequency of appearance of each unique configuration. Each batch of samples defines a subspace ($\\mathcal{S^{(k)}}$). Next, the molecular Hamiltonian, $H$, is projected onto subspaces:\n"
"$$\n"
"H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} = P_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} H _{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\text{ with } P_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} = \\sum_{x \\in \\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\vert x \\rangle \\langle x \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"![A flow chart showing how sampled states are used to determine ground state eigenvalues and eigenvectors.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig10.avif)\n"
"Sampling the LUCJ ansatz in the computational basis generates a pool of noisy configurations $\\tilde{\\mathcal{\\chi}}$, which are used in the post-processing routine. It involves a method called (details discussed later) _configuration recovery_ to probabilistically correct configurations with incorrect electron numbers. Configurations only with correct electron numbers $\\tilde{\\mathcal{\\chi}}_{R}$ are then subsampled and distributed into multiple batches based on the frequency of appearance of each unique configuration. Each batch of samples defines a subspace ($\\mathcal{S^{(k)}}$). Next, the molecular Hamiltonian, $H$, is projected onto subspaces:\n"
"$$\n"
"H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} = P_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} H _{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\text{ with } P_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} = \\sum_{x \\in \\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\vert x \\rangle \\langle x \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each projected Hamiltonian $H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}}$ is then fed into an Eigensolver, where it is diagonalized to compute eigenvalues and eigenvectors to reconstruct an eigenstate. In this lesson, we project and diagonalize the Hamiltonian using the `qiskit-addon-sqd` package which uses the Davidson's method from PySCF for diagonalization.\n"
msgstr "Setiap Hamiltonian yang diunjurkan $H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}}$ kemudian dimasukkan ke dalam Penyelesai Eigen, di mana ia didiagonalisasikan untuk mengira nilai eigen dan vektor eigen bagi membina semula keadaan eigen. Dalam pelajaran ini, kita mengunjurkan dan mendiagonalisasikan Hamiltonian menggunakan pakej `qiskit-addon-sqd` yang menggunakan kaedah Davidson dari PySCF untuk diagonalisasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\vert \\psi^{(k)} \\rangle = E^{(k)} \\vert \\psi^{(k)} \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\vert \\psi^{(k)} \\rangle = E^{(k)} \\vert \\psi^{(k)} \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We then collect the lowest eigenvalue (energy) from the batches, and also compute average orbital occupancy, $\\text{n}$. The average occupancy information is used in the configuration recovery step to probabilistically correct noise configurations.\n"
msgstr "Kita kemudian mengumpul nilai eigen terendah (tenaga) dari batch, dan juga mengira purata penghunian orbital, $\\text{n}$. Maklumat penghunian purata digunakan dalam langkah pemulihan konfigurasi untuk membetulkan konfigurasi berhingar secara kebarangkalian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we explain the self-consistent configuration recovery loop in detail and show concrete code examples to implement the above-mentioned steps to estimate the ground state energy of $N_2$ Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, kita menjelaskan gelung pemulihan konfigurasi konsisten diri secara terperinci dan menunjukkan contoh kod konkrit untuk melaksanakan langkah-langkah yang disebutkan di atas bagi menganggar tenaga keadaan tanah Hamiltonian $N_2$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.1 Configuration recovery: overview {#41-configuration-recovery-overview}"
msgstr "4.1 Pemulihan konfigurasi: gambaran keseluruhan {#41-configuration-recovery-overview}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each bit in a bitstring (Slater determinant) represents a spin orbital. The right half of a bitstring represents spin-up orbitals, and the left half represents spin-down orbitals. A `1` means the orbital is occupied by an electron, and a `0` means the orbital is empty. We know the correct number of particles (both up-spin electron and down-spin electron) a priori. Suppose we have a determinant $x$ with $N_x$ electrons (that is, there are $N_x$ numbers of $1$s in the bitstring) in it. The correct number of particles is $N$. If $N_x \\neq N$, then we know that the bitstring is corrupted by noise. The self-consistent configuration routine attempts to correct the bitstring by probabilistically flipping $|N_x - N|$ bits by leveraging average orbital occupancy information. The average orbital occupancy ($n$) tells us how likely an orbital be occupied by an electron. If $N_x < N$, we have fewer electrons and need to flip some $0$s to $1$s and vice versa.\n"
msgstr "Setiap bit dalam bitstring (penentu Slater) mewakili orbital spin. Separuh kanan bitstring mewakili orbital spin-atas, dan separuh kiri mewakili orbital spin-bawah. `1` bermaksud orbital diduduki oleh elektron, dan `0` bermaksud orbital kosong. Kita mengetahui bilangan zarah yang betul (kedua-dua elektron spin-atas dan elektron spin-bawah) secara priori. Andaikan kita mempunyai penentu $x$ dengan $N_x$ elektron (iaitu, terdapat $N_x$ bilangan $1$ dalam bitstring) di dalamnya. Bilangan zarah yang betul ialah $N$. Jika $N_x \\neq N$, maka kita tahu bahawa bitstring telah rosak akibat hingar. Rutin konfigurasi konsisten kendiri cuba membetulkan bitstring dengan membalikkan secara kebarangkalian $|N_x - N|$ bit dengan memanfaatkan maklumat purata pekerjaan orbital. Purata pekerjaan orbital ($n$) memberitahu kita betapa mungkinnya sesuatu orbital diduduki oleh elektron. Jika $N_x < N$, kita mempunyai lebih sedikit elektron dan perlu membalikkan sesetengah $0$ kepada $1$ dan sebaliknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The probability of flipping can be $|x[i] - avg\\_occupancy[i]|$ for `i`-th spin orbital. In [\\[2\\]](#references), the authors used a weighted probability of flipping using modified ReLU function.\n"
msgstr "Kebarangkalian membalikkan boleh menjadi $|x[i] - avg\\_occupancy[i]|$ untuk orbital spin ke-`i`. Dalam [\\[2\\]](#references), penulis menggunakan kebarangkalian membalikkan berbobot menggunakan fungsi ReLU yang dimodifikasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"    w(y) = \\begin{cases}\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"    w(y) = \\begin{cases}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    \\delta \\frac{y}{h} & \\text{if }  y \\leq h\\\\ \\nonumber\n"
msgstr "    \\delta \\frac{y}{h} & \\text{if }  y \\leq h\\\\ \\nonumber\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    \\delta + (1 - \\delta) \\frac{y - h}{1 - h} & \\text{if } y > h\n"
msgstr "    \\delta + (1 - \\delta) \\frac{y - h}{1 - h} & \\text{if } y > h\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here $h$ defines the location of \"corner\" of the ReLU function, and the parameter $\\delta$ defines the value of the ReLU function at the corner. For $\\delta = 0$, $w$ becomes true ReLU function, and for $\\delta >0$, it becomes _modified_ ReLU. In the paper, the authors used $\\delta = 0.01$ and $h =$ number of alpha (or beta) particles/number of alpha (or beta) spin orbitals $= N/M$ (filling factor).\n"
msgstr "Di sini $h$ mentakrifkan lokasi \"sudut\" fungsi ReLU, dan parameter $\\delta$ mentakrifkan nilai fungsi ReLU pada sudut. Untuk $\\delta = 0$, $w$ menjadi fungsi ReLU sebenar, dan untuk $\\delta >0$, ia menjadi ReLU _yang dimodifikasi_. Dalam makalah tersebut, penulis menggunakan $\\delta = 0.01$ dan $h =$ bilangan zarah alfa (atau beta)/bilangan orbital spin alfa (atau beta) $= N/M$ (faktor pengisian).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The average orbital occupancy ($n$) is not known a priori. The first iteration of the ground state estimation starts with configurations with only correct particle numbers in both spin species. After the first iteration, we have an estimate of the ground state, and using the estimate, we can construct the first guess of $n$. This guess of $n$ is used to recover configurations, run the next iteration of ground state estimation, and self-consistently refine the guess of $n$. The process repeats until the a stopping criterion is met.\n"
msgstr "Penghunian orbital purata ($n$) tidak diketahui terlebih dahulu. Iterasi pertama anggaran keadaan tanah bermula dengan konfigurasi yang hanya mempunyai bilangan zarah yang betul dalam kedua-dua spesies spin. Selepas iterasi pertama, kita mempunyai anggaran keadaan tanah, dan menggunakan anggaran tersebut, kita boleh membina tekaan pertama $n$. Tekaan $n$ ini digunakan untuk memulihkan konfigurasi, menjalankan iterasi anggaran keadaan tanah seterusnya, dan menghalusi tekaan $n$ secara konsisten diri. Proses ini berulang sehingga kriteria berhenti dipenuhi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the following example for $N = 2$ and $x = |1000\\rangle$ ($N_x = 1$). We need to flip one of the 0s to 1 to correct it for particle numbers, and the choices are `1100`, `1010`, and `1001`. Based on the probability of flipping, one of the choices will be selected as _recovered configuration_ (or the bitstring with correct number of particles).\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan contoh berikut untuk $N = 2$ dan $x = |1000\\rangle$ ($N_x = 1$). Kita perlu membalikkan salah satu daripada 0 kepada 1 untuk membetulkannya untuk bilangan zarah, dan pilihannya ialah `1100`, `1010`, dan `1001`. Berdasarkan kebarangkalian membalikkan, salah satu daripada pilihan tersebut akan dipilih sebagai _konfigurasi yang dipulihkan_ (atau bitstring dengan bilangan zarah yang betul).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose in the first iteration we run two batches, and the estimated ground states from them are:\n"
msgstr "Andaikan dalam iterasi pertama kita menjalankan dua batch, dan keadaan tanah yang dianggar daripada mereka ialah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\\nonumber\n"
"    \\text{Batch0: } \\vert \\psi \\rangle &= 0.8 \\times \\vert 1001 \\rangle + 0.6 \\times \\vert 0110 \\rangle \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"    \\text{Batch1: } \\vert \\psi \\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\left( \\vert 1001 \\rangle + \\vert 0101 \\rangle + \\vert 0110 \\rangle \\right) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\\nonumber\n"
"    \\text{Batch0: } \\vert \\psi \\rangle &= 0.8 \\times \\vert 1001 \\rangle + 0.6 \\times \\vert 0110 \\rangle \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"    \\text{Batch1: } \\vert \\psi \\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\left( \\vert 1001 \\rangle + \\vert 0101 \\rangle + \\vert 0110 \\rangle \\right) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the computational basis states and their amplitudes, we can compute probability of electron occupancies (in short _occupancies_) per spin-orbital (qubit) (note that probability = |amplitude|$^2$). Below we tabulate qubit-wise occupancies for each bitstring appearing in the estimated ground state and compute total orbital occupancy for a batch. Note that, as per Qiskit ordering convention, the right most bit represents qubit-0 (Q0), and the left most bit represents Q3.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan keadaan asas pengkomputeran dan amplitudnya, kita boleh mengira kebarangkalian penghunian elektron (ringkasnya _penghunian_) per orbital spin (qubit) (perhatikan bahawa kebarangkalian = |amplitud|$^2$). Di bawah kita menyusun penghunian mengikut qubit untuk setiap bitstring yang muncul dalam keadaan tanah yang dianggar dan mengira penghunian orbital keseluruhan untuk setiap batch. Perhatikan bahawa, menurut konvensyen susunan Qiskit, bit paling kanan mewakili qubit-0 (Q0), dan bit paling kiri mewakili Q3.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Occupancy (Batch0):\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"|    1001   |   0.64   |    0.0   |    0.0   |   0.64   |\n"
"|    0110   |    0.0   |   0.36   |   0.36   |    0.0   |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch0)_ | **0.64** | **0.36** | **0.36** | **0.64** |\n"
msgstr ""
"Penghunian (Batch0):\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"|    1001   |   0.64   |    0.0   |    0.0   |   0.64   |\n"
"|    0110   |    0.0   |   0.36   |   0.36   |    0.0   |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch0)_ | **0.64** | **0.36** | **0.36** | **0.64** |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Occupancy (Batch1)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"|    1001   |    0.33   |   0.00   |   0.00   |    0.33   |\n"
"|    0101   |    0.0   |   0.33   |   0.00   |    0.33   |\n"
"|    0110   |    0.0   |   0.33   |   0.33   |    0.00   |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch1)_ | **0.33** | **0.66** | **0.33** | **0.66** |\n"
msgstr ""
"Penghunian (Batch1)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"|    1001   |    0.33   |   0.00   |   0.00   |    0.33   |\n"
"|    0101   |    0.0   |   0.33   |   0.00   |    0.33   |\n"
"|    0110   |    0.0   |   0.33   |   0.33   |    0.00   |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch1)_ | **0.33** | **0.66** | **0.33** | **0.66** |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Occupancy (average across batches)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"| **n** _(Batch0)_ | 0.64 | 0.36 | 0.36 | 0.64 |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch1)_ | 0.33 | 0.66 | 0.33 | 0.66 |\n"
"| **n** _(average)_ | **0.49** | **0.51** | **0.35** | **0.65** |\n"
msgstr ""
"Penghunian (purata merentasi batch)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"| **n** _(Batch0)_ | 0.64 | 0.36 | 0.36 | 0.64 |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch1)_ | 0.33 | 0.66 | 0.33 | 0.66 |\n"
"| **n** _(purata)_ | **0.49** | **0.51** | **0.35** | **0.65** |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the average orbital occupancy computed above, we can find the probabilities of flip for different orbitals in the configuration $x = \\vert 1000 \\rangle$. As the orbital represented by Q3 is already occupied and need not to be flipped, we set its p(flip) to $0$. For the remaining orbitals, which are unoccupied, the probability of flip is $\\vert x[i] - \\text{n}[i] \\vert$ each. Along with p(flip), we also compute the probability weight associated with flipping using the modified ReLU function described above.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan penghunian orbital purata yang dikira di atas, kita boleh mencari kebarangkalian membalikkan untuk orbital berbeza dalam konfigurasi $x = \\vert 1000 \\rangle$. Kerana orbital yang diwakili oleh Q3 sudah dihuni dan tidak perlu dibalikkan, kita tetapkan p(balik) kepada $0$. Untuk orbital yang tidak dihuni yang selebihnya, kebarangkalian membalikkan ialah $\\vert x[i] - \\text{n}[i] \\vert$ masing-masing. Bersama-sama dengan p(balik), kita juga mengira pemberat kebarangkalian yang berkaitan dengan membalikkan menggunakan fungsi ReLU yang dimodifikasi yang diterangkan di atas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Probability of flip ($x = \\vert 1000 \\rangle$, $\\delta = 0.01$, $h = N/M = 2/4 = 0.50$)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"| p(flip) ($\\vert x[i] - \\text{n}[i] \\vert$) | 0 | 0.51 | 0.35 | 0.65 |\n"
"| w(p(flip)) | 0 | 0.03 | 0.007 | 0.31 |\n"
msgstr ""
"Kebarangkalian membalikkan ($x = \\vert 1000 \\rangle$, $\\delta = 0.01$, $h = N/M = 2/4 = 0.50$)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"| p(balik) ($\\vert x[i] - \\text{n}[i] \\vert$) | 0 | 0.51 | 0.35 | 0.65 |\n"
"| w(p(balik)) | 0 | 0.03 | 0.007 | 0.31 |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, using weighted probabilities above, we can flip one of the unoccupied Q2, Q1, and Q0 orbitals. Based on the values above, Q0 will be flipped most likely, and a possible recovered configuration can be $\\vert \\text{1001} \\rangle$.\n"
"![A diagram of configuration recovery.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig11.avif)\n"
"The complete self-consistent configuration recovery process can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, menggunakan kebarangkalian berbobot di atas, kita boleh membalikkan salah satu daripada orbital Q2, Q1, dan Q0 yang tidak dihuni. Berdasarkan nilai di atas, Q0 paling berkemungkinan dibalikkan, dan konfigurasi yang dipulihkan yang mungkin ialah $\\vert \\text{1001} \\rangle$.\n"
"![Gambar rajah pemulihan konfigurasi.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig11.avif)\n"
"Proses pemulihan konfigurasi konsisten diri yang lengkap boleh diringkaskan seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**First iteration:** Suppose the bitstrings (configurations or Slater determinants) generated by the quantum computer form a set $\\widetilde{\\chi}$, which includes both configurations with correct ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct}$) and incorrect ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{incorrect}$) number of particles in each spin sector.\n"
"1. Configurations from ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct}$) are randomly sampled to create batches $(\\mathcal{S}^{(1)}, \\cdots, \\mathcal{S}^{(K)})$ of vectors for subspace projection. The number of batches and samples in each batch are user defined parameters. The larger the number of samples in each batch, the larger the subspace dimension and more computationally demanding the diagonalization becomes. On the other hand, too small number of samples may miss the ground state support vectors and lead to incorrect estimation.\n"
"2. Run the eigenstate solver (that is, projection onto subspace and diagonalization) on the batches and obtain approximate eigenstates. $|\\psi^{(1)}\\rangle, \\cdots, |\\psi^{(K)}\\rangle$.\n"
"3. From the approximate eigenstates construct the first guess for $n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Iterasi pertama:** Andaikan bitstring (konfigurasi atau determinan Slater) yang dijana oleh komputer kuantum membentuk set $\\widetilde{\\chi}$, yang merangkumi kedua-dua konfigurasi dengan bilangan zarah yang betul ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct}$) dan tidak betul ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{incorrect}$) dalam setiap sektor spin.\n"
"1. Konfigurasi dari ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct}$) disampling secara rawak untuk mencipta batch $(\\mathcal{S}^{(1)}, \\cdots, \\mathcal{S}^{(K)})$ vektor untuk unjuran subruang. Bilangan batch dan sampel dalam setiap batch adalah parameter yang ditentukan pengguna. Semakin besar bilangan sampel dalam setiap batch, semakin besar dimensi subruang dan semakin menuntut pengiraan diagonalisasinya. Di sisi lain, bilangan sampel yang terlalu kecil mungkin terlepas vektor sokongan keadaan tanah dan mengakibatkan anggaran yang salah.\n"
"2. Jalankan penyelesai keadaan eigen (iaitu, unjuran ke atas subruang dan diagonalisasi) pada batch dan dapatkan keadaan eigen anggaran. $|\\psi^{(1)}\\rangle, \\cdots, |\\psi^{(K)}\\rangle$.\n"
"3. Daripada keadaan eigen anggaran bina tekaan pertama untuk $n$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Subsequent iterations:**\n"
"1. Using $n$ correct the configurations with wrong particle number in $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{incorrect}$. Suppose we name them $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct\\_new}$. Then, $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{recovered} (\\widetilde{\\chi}_{R}) = \\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct} \\cup \\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct\\_new}$ forms the new set of configurations with correct particle numbers.\n"
"2. $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{R}$ is sampled to create batches $\\mathcal{S}^{(1)}, \\cdots, \\mathcal{S}^{(K)}$.\n"
"3. Eigenstate solver runs with new batches and generates new estimates of ground states $|\\psi^{(1)}\\rangle, \\cdots, |\\psi^{(K)}\\rangle$.\n"
"4. From the approximate eigenstates construct refined guess for $n$.\n"
"5. If the stopping criterion is not met, go back to step `2.1`.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Iterasi berikutnya:**\n"
"1. Menggunakan $n$ betulkan konfigurasi dengan bilangan zarah yang salah dalam $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{incorrect}$. Andaikan kita menamakannya $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct\\_new}$. Kemudian, $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{recovered} (\\widetilde{\\chi}_{R}) = \\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct} \\cup \\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct\\_new}$ membentuk set konfigurasi baharu dengan bilangan zarah yang betul.\n"
"2. $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{R}$ disampling untuk mencipta batch $\\mathcal{S}^{(1)}, \\cdots, \\mathcal{S}^{(K)}$.\n"
"3. Penyelesai keadaan eigen dijalankan dengan batch baharu dan menjana anggaran keadaan tanah baharu $|\\psi^{(1)}\\rangle, \\cdots, |\\psi^{(K)}\\rangle$.\n"
"4. Daripada keadaan eigen anggaran bina tekaan yang dihalusi untuk $n$.\n"
"5. Jika kriteria berhenti tidak dipenuhi, kembali ke langkah `2.1`.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.2 Ground state estimation {#42-ground-state-estimation}"
msgstr "4.2 Anggaran keadaan tanah {#42-ground-state-estimation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we will transform the counts into a bitstring matrix and probability array for post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, kita akan mengubah kiraan kepada matriks bitstring dan array kebarangkalian untuk pasca-pemprosesan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each row in the matrix represents one unique bitstring. Since qubits are indexed from the right of a bitstring in Qiskit, column ``0`` represents qubit ``N-1``, and column ``N-1`` represents qubit ``0``, where ``N`` is the number of qubits.\n"
msgstr "Setiap baris dalam matriks mewakili satu bitstring unik. Kerana qubit diindeks dari kanan bitstring dalam Qiskit, lajur ``0`` mewakili qubit ``N-1``, dan lajur ``N-1`` mewakili qubit ``0``, di mana ``N`` ialah bilangan qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The alpha orbitals are represented in the column index range ``(N, N/2]`` (right half), and the beta orbitals are represented in the column range ``(N/2, 0]`` (left half).\n"
msgstr "Orbital alfa diwakili dalam julat indeks lajur ``(N, N/2]`` (separuh kanan), dan orbital beta diwakili dalam julat lajur ``(N/2, 0]`` (separuh kiri).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are a few user-controlled options which are important for this technique:\n"
msgstr "Terdapat beberapa pilihan yang dikawal pengguna yang penting untuk teknik ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``iterations``: Number of self-consistent configuration recovery iterations\n"
msgstr "``iterations``: Bilangan iterasi pemulihan konfigurasi konsisten diri\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``n_batches``: Number of batches of configurations used by the different calls to the eigenstate solver\n"
msgstr "``n_batches``: Bilangan batch konfigurasi yang digunakan oleh panggilan berbeza kepada penyelesai keadaan eigen\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``samples_per_batch``: Number of unique configurations to include in each batch\n"
msgstr "``samples_per_batch``: Bilangan konfigurasi unik untuk disertakan dalam setiap batch\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``max_davidson_cycles``: Maximum number of Davidson cycles run by each eigensolver\n"
msgstr "``max_davidson_cycles``: Bilangan kitaran Davidson maksimum yang dijalankan oleh setiap penyelesai eigen\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.3 Discussion of results {#43-discussion-of-results}"
msgstr "4.3 Perbincangan keputusan {#43-discussion-of-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first plot shows that after a few iterations we estimate the ground state energy within ~24 mH (chemical accuracy is typically accepted to be 1 kcal/mol $\\approx$ 1.6 mH). The second plot shows the average occupancy of each spatial orbital after the final iteration. We can see that both the spin-up and spin-down electrons occupy the first five orbitals with high probability in our solutions.\n"
msgstr "Plot pertama menunjukkan bahawa selepas beberapa iterasi kita menganggar tenaga keadaan tanah dalam ~24 mH (ketepatan kimia biasanya diterima sebagai 1 kcal/mol $\\approx$ 1.6 mH). Plot kedua menunjukkan purata penghunian setiap orbital ruang selepas iterasi terakhir. Kita dapat melihat bahawa kedua-dua elektron spin atas dan spin bawah menghuni lima orbital pertama dengan kebarangkalian tinggi dalam penyelesaian kita.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Although the estimated ground state energy is decent, it is not within the chemical accuracy limit ($\\pm \\approx 1.6$ mH). This gap can be attributed to the small subspace dimension we used above for projection and diagonalization. As we used `samples_per_batch=500`, the subspace is spanned by max $500$ vectors, which is missing vectors from ground state support. Increasing the `samples_per_batch` parameter should improve the accuracy at the expense of more classical compute resources and runtime.\n"
msgstr "Walaupun tenaga keadaan tanah yang dianggar adalah baik, ia tidak dalam had ketepatan kimia ($\\pm \\approx 1.6$ mH). Jurang ini boleh dikaitkan dengan dimensi subruang kecil yang kita gunakan di atas untuk unjuran dan diagonalisasi. Kerana kita menggunakan `samples_per_batch=500`, subruang dicakupi oleh maksimum $500$ vektor, yang ketinggalan vektor dari sokongan keadaan tanah. Meningkatkan parameter `samples_per_batch` harus meningkatkan ketepatan dengan mengorbankan lebih banyak sumber pengkomputeran klasik dan masa jalan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/qda-4-sqd-implementation/extracted-outputs/8cd90034-6ef3-41bd-a847-c115cade82f7-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/qda-4-sqd-implementation/extracted-outputs/8cd90034-6ef3-41bd-a847-c115cade82f7-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exercise for the reader {#exercise-for-the-reader}"
msgstr "Latihan untuk pembaca {#exercise-for-the-reader}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Progressively increase the `samples_per_batch` parameter (for example, from $1000$ to $10000$ at a step of $1000$; permitted my your computer's memory) and compare the estimated ground state energies.\n"
msgstr "Tingkatkan parameter `samples_per_batch` secara beransur-ansur (sebagai contoh, dari $1000$ hingga $10000$ dengan langkah $1000$; bergantung pada memori komputer anda) dan bandingkan tenaga keadaan tanah yang dianggar.\n"

